course: dictionary
lesson: 10041
title: Terracotta: a clay and a colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one job. «Terracotta» can be a noun, the name of a material, or an adjective, a word that describes something. The words around it tell you which one it is.
explain: Terracotta is a reddish-brown clay that has been baked hard. Flowerpots, roof tiles and statues are often made from it, so it is a material you can hold.
explain: When you see «a terracotta pot», the word tells you the colour of the pot: orange-brown. The word before the thing it describes is a strong clue.
explain: «The Terracotta Army» has capital letters, so it is a special name. It means a huge group of clay soldier statues buried with an ancient emperor in China.
fact: Terracotta is a reddish-brown clay that has been baked hard.
fact: As an adjective, terracotta describes an orange-brown colour, as in «a terracotta pot».
fact: «The Terracotta Army» is a huge group of clay soldier statues buried with an ancient emperor in China.
fact: In 1974 farmers digging a well near Xi'an found the Terracotta Army.
fact: Each clay soldier has a different face and hairstyle, with details added by hand.
exercise: «Farmers digging a well found the Terracotta Army in 1974.» Who found it? | Children on a school trip | *Farmers digging a well | The First Emperor | Roman soldiers
exercise: «The garden had a terracotta pot full of red flowers.» What colour is the pot? | Sky grey | Bright blue | *Orange-brown | Pure white
exercise: What is terracotta as a material? | A bright green plant | *A reddish-brown clay that has been baked hard | A loud drum | A long river in China
test: «The First Emperor was buried with about 8,000 life-size clay soldiers.» What are the soldiers made of? | Glass | Wood | *Clay | Gold
test: Why are terracotta pots common in gardens? | *They let air and water through | They are made of glass and never break | They are very heavy and hard to move | Gold is too expensive for flowers
exam: In «Terracotta is a reddish-brown clay», what kind of word is terracotta? | A verb, an action word | An adjective, describing a colour | *A noun, a name for the clay | A number
